{
	"description": "Takes a task to a merged pull request in a GitHub repository: plans the change and asks a person to approve the plan, writes it on the run's branch and runs the repository's own checks on it, has a panel of reviewers review it at once and, as a person or the team's standing rules decide, fixes the blockers they find, reviewing each fix's changes again, opens a pull request, waits for its checks and fixes what fails, then asks a person whether to merge the commit that passed, and merges it once the base branch's required checks pass. Before it opens the pull request, a verifier checks the change against the task's done-when clauses and runs the acceptance checks the plan wrote, sending what fails to be fixed as a person or the team's standing rules decide. The run ends once its change is merged. A finding outside the changes under review becomes a follow-up task and does not hold the pull request. A review that still finds blockers after three rounds leaves the branch for a person, and checks that still fail after their last round leave the branch for one. A merge waits while the base branch's required checks fail, and asks again if they still fail after its wait. Runs merge into a base branch one after the other, in the order they reached their merge; a branch the base moved past is brought up to date by merging the base in (a conflict the agent cannot resolve goes to a person), its checks and CI run again, and the merge is asked again.",
	"repository": true,
